 # CHANGELOG
 
+## v0.6.1.6 — 2026-08-21
+
+### Requested
+
+- Remove the remaining global coordination assumptions inherited from physical mouse ownership now that runtime point actions are internal per-client actions.
+- Make clients independent: unrelated SELL, trade, REC and P1/P2/P3 work must not wait for a shared input resource.
+- Require authoritative AutoFight OFF before **both Mount and StartPath**, reusing the existing two-stop/reset Travel Guard.
+
+### Changed — independent client ownership
+
+- Remove global hidden-action busy/owner/recording state. Generic point dispatch is scoped to the target client and never consults the MAIN↔CON transaction lock.
+- Replace the old hidden sequence lease naming with a business-only Trade Workflow Lock. It preserves transaction order but does not block unrelated PIDs.
+- Remove the rule that any account in SELL item phase blocks the trade coordinator.
+- Scope recorder blocking: Sell blocks its PID; TradeChild blocks the recorded child plus its MAIN; TradeMain blocks its MAIN. Unrelated clients continue.
+- Replace global MAIN→CON priority passes with local `P1 → P2 → P3` evaluation per account.
+- Fan out snapshot `ReadState` calls concurrently per PID, then merge/observe on the controller thread. This removes the old `N × Bridge timeout` polling behavior without moving UI/profile-mutating FSM code onto worker threads.
+
+### Fixed — Mount movement guard
+
+- v0.6.1.5 guaranteed the Travel Guard before `StartPath`, but the first Mount attempt in robust travel could still be sent while AutoFight was ON.
+- The central action gate now applies the exact same `EnsureAutoFightOffForTravel` proof to `Action::Mount` and `Action::StartPath`.
+- Existing recovery policy is unchanged: Stop #1 → verify, Stop #2 → verify, if still ON run one AUTO/Attack reset, then repeat until a fresh authoritative snapshot proves OFF.
+- Existing `AutoPath && AutoFight` conflict latch remains fail-closed and also forbids Mount until recovery completes.
+
+### Preserved
+
+- Client Freeze, F4 global manual pause, death/revive lifecycle, route ownership reset, FIFO/re-lock, stable `FreeBagSpace` proof, trade step/repeat/group semantics and InputSync press/release transport.
+- `WH_GETMESSAGE` Bridge integration is not the removed low-level mouse hook. F8/REC still read manual input for configuration only.
+
+### Verification status
+
+- `tools/verify_v0616_logic.py`: PASS locally.
+- Eight native pure C++ logic test groups: PASS locally.
+- Windows MSVC x64 CI and live-client behavior: pending until recorded.
+
